WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.440
"But my duty must be done, even alone"

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.080
"For the children I knew, bless their souls"

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.560
Anri and Horace

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.580
Two of the only children to have ever escaped the clutches of aldrich

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.460
The man eater

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.180
now, undead and unkindled

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.060
they stride willingly back into his grasp

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.800
"Oh hello"

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.840
"How do you do?"

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.720
"I am Anri of Astora"

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.900
"Unkindled like you"

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.280
"Are you too in search of The Lords of Cinder?"

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.320
"We seek the cathedral"

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.580
"Home of the grim Aldrich"

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.360
"We may go our seperate ways now"

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.080
"But we are both seekers of lords"

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.000
"The next time we cross paths"

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.280
"One of us may find the other in a time of need"

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.660
"Oh yes! Horace."

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.100
"He's not very talkative"

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.700
"But don't think Ill of him"

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.720
"He is an upstanding kind hearted knight"

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.000
"Fine partner for this grueling journey"

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.220
"Please stop this!"

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.320
"You've gone hollow, have you?"

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.620
"Than I shall put you to rest!"

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.900
"Horace, join me"

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.540
"And may the flames watch over us"

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.260
"Oh Horace, Why?"

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.540
"Don't leave me"

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:28.860
"Not you"

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.200
"Not like the others"

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.440
"Oh Horace"

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.380
"Horace..."

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.440
"Everyone"

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.120
"Forgive me"

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.540
"I was weak on my own"

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.940
From this, we learn of Anri's fear

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.380
Fear that those by her side, will die

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.460
You can imagine this fear would have been born

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.900
From her childhood in the cathedral

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.020
As the children along side her, were sacrificed

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.620
So, if Horace lives

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.420
Then he remains a source of strength to her

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.680
For a little longer

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.060
Anri's blue sentinel...

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.180
"Without his help, I would have cursed 
this onerous duty long ago"

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.260
At the end of The Road of Sacrifices sits the cathedral of the deep

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.000
And deep within the cathedral

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.860
Is the monumental coffin of Aldrich the Man Eater

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:34.480
"A right and proper cleric, only he developed a habit of devouring men"

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:41.140
"He ate so many that he bloated like a drowned pig"

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.780
"And softened into sludge"

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.960
"So they him stuck in the cathedral of the deep"

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.600
Back then the Cathedral of the Deep was a holy place

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.780
Full of god fearing deacons devoted to the way of white

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.500
And to the linking of the fire

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.980
And it was imperative that the fire be linked

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.220
For thats the way its always been

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.120
At the end of every cycle

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.520
A powerful being must be sacrificed

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.000
To keep the flame lit

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.340
The cathedral

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.740
A place of sacrifice

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.080
May have well been designed for this

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.960
So it came to be that a saint named Aldrich was sacrificed

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:25.060
"And they made him a Lord of Cinder, not for virtue, but for might"

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.780
"Such is a lord, I suppose"

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.300
The fire doesn't care if you've consumed men, women, children...

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.700
If that's made you more powerful, then all the better

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:42.120
So Aldrich, this terrible, gluttonous saint, must have been powerful indeed

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.820
The deacons tended to the flame

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:49.200
And slowly, they were corrupted by the evil, they were tending to

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.620
Eventually, of course, even this fire faded

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.400
The world darkened

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.680
But this time, no one stepped forward to link the fire

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.320
So the world continued to darken

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.780
Till the firelink bell tolled

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.880
Lords of old rose from their graves

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.460
Aldrich among them, brought back to link the fire again

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.760
These lords came back, clinging to to life and they were loathe to let it go

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.160
So they refused to sit their thrones once more

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.840
And with this refusal came the unkindled

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.280
ashen undead, each tied to a lord

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.480
Siegward to Yhorm, the giants friend

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.400
Hawkwood to the legion he abandoned

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.480
And Anri to Aldrich

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.900
Whose clutches she escaped as a child

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.700
After her and Horace escape the Cathedral of the Deep

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.480
They went on to do great things

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.720
Anri found herself drawn to the land of Astora

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.620
As it was being destroyed by the spirit of Evil Eye

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.100
With nothing but a dull blade

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:52.960
And luck

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.720
She defeated the creature

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.920
Horace killed a corrupt executioner

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.480
He stripped the executioner of his armor

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.180
And gave it a new legacy

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.820
He would become a blue sentinal

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.400
Protecting the weak from Rosaria's fingers

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.460
These red phantoms, who take the tongues of those they kill in battle

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.900
I'd say that explains the voice

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.800
And death could not keep either of them

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.540
With Horace undead and Anri unkindled

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.620
They rejoin forces and

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.900
Fight their way back into this horrific home, they left as children

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.600
To fight a familiar evil that rises again

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:37.820
And alas, Anri and Horace find themselves staring into an empty coffin

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.660
"I'm well-pleased to see you safe"

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.880
"We've reached the Cathedral of the Deep"

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.520
"But Aldrich's coffin was empty"

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.160
"The man-eater must have left for his true home"

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.580
"The little doll in the empty coffin told me"

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.760
Wherever you go, the moon still sets in Irithyll

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.460
Wherever you may be

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.740
Irithyll is your home

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.900
"A pilgrim told me that the city lies beyond Farron Keep"

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.160
"And so becomes our destination"

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:18.700
"Oh, hello"

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.360
"How very fortunate"

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.440
"Have you seen my companion Horace?"

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:28.380
"To my shame, I was snared by a trap and we've become seperated"

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:31.460
"I've not been able to find him since"

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.860
If you tell Anri where he is, then Anri will go to find him

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:40.920
Full of fear that she might have to confront Aldrich,

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.560
This childhood horror, alone

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.020
But a hollow remembers no one

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.420
So it is better that she go on alone

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.340
"Oh Horace"

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.900
"Where have you run off to?"

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:57.940
"Have you abandoned me?"

00:06:58.880 --> 00:06:59.640
"no..."

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.960
"What a horrible thought"

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.560
We find Anri next in the Church of Yorshka

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.560
She is alone, she is tired

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.620
You can see this in her stance

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:14.380
She is losing faith, and she is so close to Aldrich

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:17.700
Who hides behind the Pontiff, who called him home

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.260
"Oh, I thought it might be you"

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.640
"Good to see you"

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.300
"I never managed to find Horace"

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.900
"But my duty must be done, even alone"

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:31.740
"As an unkindled lord seeker"

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.520
"For the children I knew, bless their souls"

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.100
"We all have our reasons, don't we?"

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.620
Unkindled are born from the ash of undead

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.880
Who tried to link the fire in a past age

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.000
Unkindled can go hollow too

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.520
Just as Horace did, reverting to that hollowed state

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.020
Devoid of a soul

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.120
Even lords can go hollow

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.880
But it is men who are branded with the dark sign

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.380
That leaks their humanity, their soul, from them

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:05.160
Here, if you do nothing, then Anri will go hollow

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:08.020
But what if there is more to the dark sign?

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.100
To hollowing

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.540
"We pilgrims of Londor are keenly aware"

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:17.820
"That those branded by the dark sign"

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.120
"Possess something quite special"

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.560
"A pilgrim told me that the city lies beyond Farron Keep"

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.220
"Knowest thou of a maid named Anri?"

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.060
"She is hollow"

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.400
"And will join thee in wedlock"

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.380
"A fellow of mine guides her at this moment"

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.040
"When the time is ripe"

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.660
"Thou mayest make thy salutations"

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.180
"For what lord taketh no spouse?"

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:56.800
To become a lord of hollows is to embrace the curse

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.560
That mankind was given, you make it your strength

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:03.780
Not your weakness, you embrace a new identity

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.180
But you must take the sigils of others

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.300
In the name of that goal

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.460
And as you rest the flame from it's mantle

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.560
Anri kneels in the background, her purpose forgotten

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.500
In exchange for yours

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:22.020
Would you abandon your humanity for this?

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:27.740
"Why?"

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.500
"lady"

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.840
"Yuria..."

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.300
"Ah"

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.260
"You are brave indeed"

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.820
"To face your duty alone"

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.200
"I would do well to learn from you"

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.500
"May the flames guide your way"

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.860
But neither of you are alone

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.820
Together you kill the Pontiff

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.260
And together, you face Aldrich

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.120
"Ah"

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:00.680
"I thought it might be you"

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.920
"Then I am afraid Horace..."

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:05.520
"No"

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.440
"This only bolsters my resolve"

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.700
"Please, lend me your strength"

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.160
"Help me vanquish Aldrich"

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:17.400
"The man-eating fiend"

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:21.760
"Yes!"

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:24.740
"We did it!"

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:27.600
"I owe this to you"

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:29.980
"Thank you, truly"

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.360
"Horace, we've done it"

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.100
"We really have"

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:39.920
"Knows thou the name: Anri of Astora?"

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.340
"The brave girl left this, as thanks"

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.660
"Now, heed this little warning"

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:51.460
"From this little lord"

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:54.080
"Seek not the girl"

00:10:55.600 --> 00:11:00.440
"She knoweth her fate, what will become of her upon her duty's end"

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:03.940
"She would not wish thee follow her"

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:09.540
Her duty fulfilled, Anri will hollow in one of two places

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.720
If you told her where Horace hollowed

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.860
But killed him to protect her

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:20.040
Then Anri places one last prism stone and hollows alongside her companion

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.940
Her duty fulfilled

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:28.300
If Anri never found Horace, then she hollows in-front of these tiny graves

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.600
Maybe built for Horace

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.900
Or for the children, they once knew

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:37.840
So, how will your story end?

